>>
endobj
461 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (The PETROBOTS RoboTrack Grand Prix \(RoboTrack GP\) is an official tournament designed to showcase the intersection of mechanical engineering, electronic integration, and algorithmic programming. This tournament provides a competitive yet collaborative environment where students and hobbyists can apply theoretical STEM knowledge to solve real-world autonomous navigation challenges. By establishing three distinct categories which are Rookie, Expert, and Grandmaster.This tournament ensures that participants are evaluated against peers of similar technical experience and hardware capabilities. All attendees, including participants, mentors, and spectators, are expected to uphold the principles of fair play and technical honesty while adhering strictly to the regulations outlined in this manual. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 165 0 R
/T (2.0 Tournament Objective )
/E (2.0 Tournament Objective )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (The primary objective of RoboTrack GP is to challenge participants to design, build, and program a fully autonomous robot capable of navigating a complex path with speed and high precision. Beyond the technical aspect, the event aims to cultivate critical thinking and real-time problem-solving skills as teams calibrate their sensors to adapt to the specific environment and lighting conditions. Furthermore, the tournament is structured to encourage mastery of various control platforms, from modular educational kits to advanced open-source microcontrollers. Ultimately, the goal is to foster innovation and engineering excellence, rewarding teams that can achieve the most efficient balance between hardware stability and sophisticated software logic.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
