/E (To ensure that all teams have the opportunity to complete the course, a checkpoint system is implemented. A checkpoint is cleared only when the entire body of the robot has crossed the marker. If a robot loses the line, remains stationary for more than five \(5\) seconds, or moves in the wrong direction, it is considered a failure. In the event of a failure, a team member may pick up the robot and place it back at a position behind the last successfully cleared checkpoint. The timer will not be paused during this revival process.)
